    <h2>What Is the Dairy Queen Two Cheese Deluxe Stackburger?</h2>
    <p>In Dairy Queen's revamped Signature Stackburger lineup, the Two Cheese Deluxe Stackburger represents the definitive American double cheeseburger. Built with two 100% seasoned pure beef patties hot off the flat-top, this burger layers two thick slices of melted American cheese between and over the patties, finished with crisp dill pickle chips, sliced white onions, tangy yellow mustard, and Heinz ketchup on a toasted bakery bun.</p>
    <p>Unlike artisanal burgers burdened by heavy brioche buns or sweet synthetic dressings, the Two Cheese Deluxe prioritizes clean, savory execution. The dual slices of melted American cheese wrap each beef patty in gooey indulgence, while the sharp acidity of pickles and mustard cuts cleanly through the savory beef fat, delivering balanced satisfaction in every bite.</p>

    <h2>2026 Pricing, Calories &amp; Nutritional Facts</h2>
    <p>Priced at an approachable <strong>$8.29 a la carte</strong>, the Two Cheese Deluxe delivers substantial value for a premium double-patty build:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Calories:</strong> 630 cal</li>
      <li><strong>Protein:</strong> 34g of satiating protein from pure beef patties and melted cheese</li>
      <li><strong>Total Fat:</strong> 38g (16g Saturated Fat)</li>
      <li><strong>Sodium:</strong> ~1,280 mg</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Signature Stackburger Face-Off: Finding Your Ideal Build</h2>
    <p>Here is how the Two Cheese Deluxe compares across Dairy Queen's core burger selections:</p>
    <div class="table-wrap"><table class="size-table"><thead><tr><th>Burger Item</th><th>A La Carte Price</th><th>Calories</th><th>Key Build Difference</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Two Cheese Deluxe</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$8.29</td><td>630</td><td>Double patty, 2 American cheese slices, traditional ketchup/mustard</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Original Cheeseburger</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$6.39</td><td>400</td><td>Single patty, 1 cheese slice; lighter everyday lunch</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Double Cheeseburger</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$7.99</td><td>~580</td><td>Double patty, single cheese slice, standard diner dressing</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Bacon Two Cheese Deluxe</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$9.19</td><td>710</td><td>Adds thick-cut Applewood smoked bacon strips</td></tr><tr><td><strong>FlameThrower Stackburger</strong></td><td class="price-cell">$10.87</td><td>~800</td><td>Pepper Jack cheese, jalapeño bacon, fiery FlameThrower sauce</td></tr></tbody></table></div>

    <h2>Combo Strategy: How to Save on Your Meal</h2>
    <p>Ordering the Two Cheese Deluxe as an individual burger will run $8.29. If you plan to add sides, upgrading to a full meal combo or exploring seasonal coupons through the DQ Mobile App will maximize your dollar:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Combo Meal Upgrade:</strong> Adding crispy <a href="/items/regular-fries">Regular Fries</a> and a 21-oz <a href="/items/soft-drinks">Soft Drink</a> typically adds around $2.50 to $3.00—saving roughly 30% compared to purchasing fries and soda a la carte.</li>
      <li><strong>Dessert Pairing:</strong> Because 630 calories represents a hearty meal, pair the Two Cheese Deluxe with a lighter dessert such as a <a href="/items/vanilla-soft-serve-cone">Small Vanilla Soft Serve Cone</a> (170 cal · $1.79) or a <a href="/items/strawberry-sundae">Strawberry Sundae</a> (280 cal · $3.79).</li>
    </ul>

